{"name":"Fountain City","hex":"#9cd4cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural source of water; a spring.","An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow or gush as if from a fountain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain"},{"term":"city","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definition, depending on the place.","A settlement granted special status by royal charter or letters patent; traditionally, a settlement with a cathedral regardless of size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/city"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fountain City, Indiana","blocks":[{"text":"Fountain City, formerly Newport, is a town in New Garden Township, Wayne County, in the U.S. state of Indiana. The population was 714 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Fountaincity%2C_Indiana.jpg/330px-Fountaincity%2C_Indiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_City%2C_Indiana","wikidata":"Q1439902"},{"title":"Fountain City, Knoxville","blocks":[{"text":"Fountain City is a neighborhood in northern Knoxville, Tennessee, in the southeastern United States. Although not a census-designated place, the populations of the two ZIP codes that serve Fountain City— 37918 and 37912— were 36,815 and 18,695, respectively, as of the 2000 U.S. census. At the time of its annexation by the city of Knoxville in 1962, Fountain City was the largest unincorporated community in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Fountain-city-lake-tn1.jpg/330px-Fountain-city-lake-tn1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_City%2C_Knoxville","wikidata":"Q5474686"},{"title":"Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A fountain, from the Latin \"fons\", meaning source or spring, is a decorative reservoir used for discharging water. It is also a structure that jets water into the air for a decorative or dramatic effect in landscapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fountains_Collage.jpg/330px-Fountains_Collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain","wikidata":"Q483453"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Levi_Coffin_House%2C_front_and_southern_side.jpg/500px-Levi_Coffin_Hous